		<h1 class='oc-page-title '>Finance</h1>
		
	    <div class="wysiwyg-content body-content" ><p><strong>Our Responsibilities</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Budget Preparation</li>
<li>Financial, Compliance, and Tax Reporting</li>
<li>General Ledger, Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Fixed Assets, and Payroll</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Our Mission</strong><br />
The Finance Division is the collection point for most financial transactions in the County. We interface with all county departments, agencies, employees, and vendors.</p>
<p>Our objective is to deal with all our customers on a professional basis, while complying with all laws and maintaining the integrity and auditability of the County's accounting system in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, as required by WS 16-4-120(a).</p>
<p><strong>Budget Process</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>On or before May 1st of each year, all budget requests must be submitted to the County Budget Officer&nbsp;<em>(County Clerk);</em></li>
<li>On or before May 15th, the County Budget Officer presents a tentative budget to the County Commissioners;</li>
<li>Budget Hearing is held not later than the third Monday in July;</li>
<li>County Commissioners must approve a balanced budget within 24 hours of the budget hearing.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Public Information</strong><br />
Financial records, including original invoices and supporting documents, are available for public inspection in the Laramie County Finance Office. We prefer appointments; however, you may drop in at&nbsp;310 W 19th St, Suite 400, Cheyenne, WY 82001, Monday &ndash; Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. For an appointment call&nbsp;<a href="tel:13076334284" style="font-size: 1em;">307-633-4284</a>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>

